Overlay patch 0033: size screen-pass attachments from the ACQUIRED drawable
(VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK Phase 01; = sibling ports' resize-drawable-truth).
Vision Pro window-resize crash: the screen framebuffer setup receives the
caller's cached width/height but binds the freshly acquired drawable as the
color attachment. During a live resize the drawable's real size differs, so
the depth texture (sized from stale values) mismatches -> Metal render-pass
validation abort while dragging the window corner. The acquired drawable is
ground truth — derive width/height from its texture. Benign on iPhone (sizes
never change). Starship LUS path: src/graphic/Fast3D/backends/gfx_metal.cpp.

--- a/libultraship/src/graphic/Fast3D/backends/gfx_metal.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/graphic/Fast3D/backends/gfx_metal.cpp
@@ -929,6 +929,15 @@
 
     tex.texture = mCurrentDrawable->texture();
 
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0033): during a live window resize (visionOS) the
+    // acquired drawable's size can differ from the caller's cached w/h; sizing
+    // the depth attachment from stale values makes the render-pass attachments
+    // mismatch -> Metal validation abort. The drawable is the ground truth.
+    width = (uint32_t)tex.texture->width();
+    height = (uint32_t)tex.texture->height();
+#endif
+
     MTL::RenderPassDescriptor* render_pass_descriptor = MTL::RenderPassDescriptor::renderPassDescriptor();
     render_pass_descriptor->colorAttachments()->object(0)->setTexture(tex.texture);
     render_pass_descriptor->colorAttachments()->object(0)->setLoadAction(MTL::LoadActionLoad);
